window.docContents[81].resolve({"/Useless-Ramblings/The-dopamine-tank-problem/#The-Den--Useless-Ramblings--The-dopamine-tank-problem":{"contents":"If you really think about it, the canonical set of problems (the ones your mum and teacher warn you about) that arise from taking hard illegal drugs fall into several categories:\n\n1. They physically hurt you due to your physical body chemistry2. You become unable to take care of yourself / your family / society etc.3. You cannot secure a reliable, lifelong supply.\n\nAll this begs the question -- if you had a drug and a setup where these were solved, what then? Essentially, if you were to be put in a tank of endless chemical bliss, that was somehow formulated to never physically harm you, and you had no responsibilities, you were somehow guaranteed to be taken care of your entire life, and were guaranteed a lifelong stay in the tank, would that be good? Or dystopian?\n\n","context":"The Den\u0009Useless Ramblings","header":"3.4. The dopamine tank problem","id":"/Useless-Ramblings/The-dopamine-tank-problem/#The-Den--Useless-Ramblings--The-dopamine-tank-problem"}});